cff-version: 1.2.0
title: slabx-lh2
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both it and the SLAB model it extends.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Ugwiyeon
    email: lyullee@kgs.or.kr
    affiliation: Korea Gas Safety Corporation
repository-code: "https://github.com/lyullee/slabx-lh2"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Liquid hydrogen extensions to the SLAB dense-gas dispersion model, with a
  criterion that says when the downwind-marching formulation may be used. Two
  corrections carry no free parameters: water saturation below the triple
  point, where the stock treatment is wrong by a factor of 3900 at 200 K, and
  a partial coupling of the cloud width to its rise. The applicability
  diagnostic reports whether a completed run may be used at all, which the
  integral models surveyed here do not.
references:
  - type: report
    authors:
      - family-names: Ermak
        given-names: Donald L.
    title: "User's Manual for SLAB: an atmospheric dispersion model for
      denser-than-air releases"
    institution:
      name: Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory
    number: UCRL-MA-105607
    year: 1990
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Wagner
        given-names: W.
      - family-names: Riethmann
        given-names: T.
      - family-names: Feistel
        given-names: R.
      - family-names: Harvey
        given-names: A. H.
    title: "New equations for the sublimation pressure and melting pressure
      of H2O ice Ih"
    journal: Journal of Physical and Chemical Reference Data
    volume: 40
    year: 2011
    start: 043103
